{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/7337-the-problems-of-werewolves-and-space-opera","id":7337,"title":"The Problems of Werewolves and Space Opera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-10T07:51:51-08:00","id":7337,"title":"The Problems of Werewolves and Space Opera","content":"<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">This is a think-tank thread for bouncing ideas. Please help me.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When developing a Mirror shard that translated werewolves and other theriomorphs into a galactic setting, it became quickly apparent that certain elements would have to be addressed and/or outright changed. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">On one hand, how do you explain theriomorphs being present on Earth, but impossible for other alien civilizations to know or have? Saying it's only relevant to humans would be jarring at best, considering the supernatural shouldn't be a localized phenomenon restricted to our own solar system. With that in mind, how the hell do you go about developing alien theriomorphs? Would there need to be a game mechanic and formula to keep them relatively balanced? If so, how?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Another question that's been bothering me is what would happen if theriomorphs decided to create their own society; colonize a world, hang a flag, etc. How would you expand the traditions and cultural customs of the Forsaken (or any shapechanger, really) to meet the scale of an entire galaxy? We can reason that Luna encompasses all moons, rather than just Earth's, but what happens when the forsaken see alien versions of themselves in other civilizations? Would it be fair for them to conceive that Luna chooses a guardian spirit for each major world? And thus Father Wolf was Earth's designated protector?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Finally, there was the issue of whether or not to reveal shapechangers to human society. If alien cultures were at war with them, and had such beings on the front lines, wouldn't it be in the theriomorphs best interests to save humanity? If so, how would their presence affect military hardware? Would they develop starships with Spirit AIs? Able to fade in and out of the Shadow of space? What neat cultural trends would appear in human society both central and colonial?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T08:15:11-08:00","id":7358,"title":"","content":"Actually there was a TV series that went with alien werewolves<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iF9BMc3rVA0\" data-code=\"iF9BMc3rVA0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iF9BMc3rVA0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> You may want to check it out for ideas. I think the werewolves appear on the first episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T09:44:51-08:00","id":7405,"title":"","content":"I actually like the concept of localized supernatural phenomena in space opera. Seems ripe with reason to be visited by advanced civilizations.<br /> <br /> Can't you see advanced races just freaking out when they realize earth has things that can't be explained through science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:16:50-08:00","id":7517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/7337-the-problems-of-werewolves-and-space-opera?p=7405#post7405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like the concept of localized supernatural phenomena in space opera. Seems ripe with reason to be visited by advanced civilizations.<br /> <br /> Can't you see advanced races just freaking out when they realize earth has things that can't be explained through science?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, I find that boring, since it doesn't feel like there's an all encompassing truth (save that word of god favors Earth for some reason). When you go galaxy-wide, it's generally expected for the big picture to get that much bigger--that somehow everything's nebulously connected, but hidden from view. If the shadow doesn't exist outside of our world, why bother going into outer space at all? And if you aren't going into space, then why bother playing a space opera?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:30:29-08:00","id":7627,"title":"","content":"It is possible that Luna isn't all moons, but has a shifting web of political alliances with various other Moon Spirits to allow her to bestow her Auspices on the Uratha using their bodies as a proxy. This incidentally means that on some worlds where there is no moon, or where the moon refuses to ally with Luna, that Uratha will undergo the First Change as Pure from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:44:09-08:00","id":8465,"title":"","content":"My personal plan for a similar campaign is that the various supernatural templates exist among the various alien species, but their saturation in each race/culture is different.<br /> <br /> Theriomorphs exist among a number of races, with them gaining the aspects/forms of various apex predators native to their home world. There won't be any &quot;Alien Werewolves&quot; as such, but that's just because they won't turn into WOLVES.<br /> My &quot;Klingon&quot;-esqe race has fully integrated the shapechangers into society, they form a sort of religious and societal over class, because their bloodline is &quot;Blessed by the God of War&quot; giving them their powers. As far a humans are concerned, this is simply a &quot;weird alien thing&quot; that our scientists are studying on the sly (so as not to offend them and start a war) but nobody SANE makes the connection between the alien lords shape-changing and silly old myths about WEREWOLVES, pff, what kind of rube do you take me for?<br /> The Uratha are, understandably, upset and concerned about this.<br /> <br /> Another race (based heavily on the typical &quot;Gray&quot; alien) are actually almost completely overrun by vampires. Vampirism isn't NATIVE to their race, but a rather unfortunate abduction a century back (I.E. during our modern age) netted some of their sampling teams a rather unexpected and unwelcome guest. 80% of their society is now Vampiric, the other 20% being kept like cattle for food. We don't know about this, and instead believe that the race's hemophagic diet is natural, and their adverse reaction to sunlight a result of a nocturnal nature and a small dim home sun. Also worth note, since they all stem from a SINGLE vampiric progenitor, they are all from a single clan. The existence of other vampire clans is unknown to them as of yet. <br /> Additionally, some other races MAY have native Vampirism, which will result in them having unique CLANS among them. <br /> <br /> Awakened mages will exist in all races in basically equal numbers. They all share the same watchtowers, interpret the supernal realms the same, and even have the same myth cycle about Atlantis and the world pre-fall. This disturbs them greatly, but also reassures them... Somewhat.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the True Fae steal from all races, the Pyros that allows a demiurge to create Prometheans is universal, as is the underworld and the Geists that strive to escape death by bonding with a Sin-Eater, and the God Machine and it's fallen Angels. I think, for my own purposes, Mummies will be the one wild card, in that the rite of return is a single very specific ritual so I'm going to say ONLY the lords of Irem discovered it. So, no alien mummies, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, that's just my take for my own campaign","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T18:35:18-08:00","id":8523,"title":"","content":"Agreeable. I'm not concerned about werewolves being all over the galaxy, but moreso the <i>concept</i> of half-spirit beings, creatures that are part of two realms interconnected to each other since the dawn of their creation. How awesome would it be to come across a krogan &quot;were-threshermaw&quot;? Or a vulcan &quot;were-byakhee&quot;?<br /> <br /> As for Luna, I'm not talking about the spirit of <i>Earth's</i> moon, I'm talking about the spirit of <b><i>Moons.</i></b> A god-like spirit who leads all lunar choirs in united song. Each moon is an avatar of this spirit, unique to the planet it watches over, with different names and ideals, but all similar in their connection to the celestial symbol they collectively represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T05:17:53-08:00","id":8734,"title":"","content":"You don't need to get into if all moons are part of the same moon. Even if the spirit world is a universal thing, and even if the gauntlet that separates it from the physical is everywhere, and even if shifters are something that happens on every planet with intelligent life, and even if the spirits of all moons are a part of the same choir... there's no reason why the various shifters would have similar origins.<br /> <br /> As for the reveal, Werewolves are not known for being amazingly proactive when it comes to what is outside their territories. The &quot;what is in their best interests&quot; argument really only applies on a pack by pack basis, not to Werewolves as a whole.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T08:52:14-08:00","id":9735,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I can get behind theriomorphs not all being lunar-based... but how would it be best approached when trying to balance out shapechangers and their &quot;power source&quot; as it were?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T20:10:24-08:00","id":11016,"title":"","content":"Well if you're talking about being vulnerable to silver, all shapeshifters are vulnerable to shapeshifters despite their origins according to War Against the Pure. Luna is the goddess of the moon, madness, and shapeshifting, she cursed all shapeshifters no matter their origin. <br /> <br /> So the hellhounds cursed by hell are vulnerable to silver, the minotaurs of helios are hurt by silver, the fishmen of mother ocean are vulnerable to silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T10:52:09-08:00","id":11420,"title":"","content":"Another point of reference is (<i>one of my all-time favorite werewolf novels EVER</i>) is Moonbane by Al Sarrantonio. Which is about aliens that look a little bit like werewolves of the &quot;<i>Werewolf's bite turns other people into werewolves variety</i>&quot; invading Earth thanks to their planet exploding and sending a meteor shower towards Earth.<br /> <br /> The Forsaken Chronicler's Guide would be of some help in designing different werewolves.<br /> <br /> With some inspiration from Apocalypse: The Mokole had many auspices, like being born among stars, etc. A alien shape shifter might have an auspice that's a combination of moons depending on how many there are. Certain &quot;Moons&quot; would have certain aspects that influence the auspice. Such as, a warrior moon, a creator moon, etc.<br /> No Moon on the planet = Auspices that deal with stars, a Sun, or many Suns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T11:05:47-08:00","id":11424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/7337-the-problems-of-werewolves-and-space-opera?p=11420#post11420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point of reference is (<i>one of my all-time favorite werewolf novels EVER</i>) is Moonbane by Al Sarrantonio. Which is about aliens that look a little bit like werewolves of the &quot;<i>Werewolf's bite turns other people into werewolves variety</i>&quot; invading Earth thanks to their planet exploding and sending a meteor shower towards Earth.<br /> <br /> The Forsaken Chronicler's Guide would be of some help in designing different werewolves.<br /> <br /> With some inspiration from Apocalypse: The Mokole had many auspices, like being born among stars, etc. A alien shape shifter might have an auspice that's a combination of moons depending on how many there are. Certain &quot;Moons&quot; would have certain aspects that influence the auspice. Such as, a warrior moon, a creator moon, etc.<br /> No Moon on the planet = Auspices that deal with stars, a Sun, or many Suns.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the solution is to copy another trait of the Mokole? You already have Unihar to deal with in the core, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T12:39:39-08:00","id":11493,"title":"","content":"I tried quoting MrParaduo but the entry got really screwy so here:<br /> <br /> \u200bTheriomorphs. Why would they be impossible on other planets? If you want them there, put them there, plenty of fiction depicts aliens as being able to shapeshift, even entire races of them. How they shapeshift is up to you. Perhaps they can turn into any living being they come across, perhaps only those they devour, maybe they can only turn a single part of their body into that of an animal, maybe they can only turn into plants, maybe they can only turn into one creature, maybe only a certain subspecies of them can transform.<br /> <br /> Balance is a touchy subject sometimes so I'll just suggest you worry about balance if you think it's important. As for mechanics, if the creatures are going to be interacting with players, you'll need them. If it's just for fanfiction or something, don't bother.<br /> <br /> For colonization, remember the Uratha don't always breed true. Sometimes it skips a generation, sometimes it never comes up. They've been around as long as humanity has, if every child a werewolf made was a werewolf, everyone would be. Or a lot more than there are, at least. As written the Uratha are the minority, and likely always will be. So if they decided to colonize a planet there'd eventually be a disparity between normal humans outnumbering the wolf blooded and werewolves. If the Forsaken set themselves up as rulers and lawmakers, when the humans had access to firearms they might decide they don't want to bother policing the spirit. And of course, the Spirit may not exist on other worlds. I suppose a feasible compromise would be that whoever created it would make some doctrine so that less problems would pop up (wolves are sacred animals, don't kill them).<br /> <br /> As for Forsaken seeing other shapeshifters, it would really depend on the situation. As it is they're a fractured lot, they don't have a universal opinion about anything except to follow in Father Wolf's footsteps, and even then not everyone is interested in that. I suppose in the end how much are you deviating from what we have now, are the Forsaken as they are, individuals thrown into a spiritual duty together, or are they going to be much more unified like the Federation?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps not related, but Glen Cook wrote a trilogy called Darkwar. It was about a wolf-woman on a planet full of wolf-people (the people are generally divided by gender and caste), and she gets some...I want to say psychic but it really was a bit spiritual, powers. Turns out most of the women in the priesthood get them, but she was really good at using the powers. They eventually came into contact with humans, but the males, who didn't usually have access to magic, had a massive technocracy on other wolf planets and rather than fighting the humans wanted to deal with them. It ended badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T12:34:52-08:00","id":12236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/7337-the-problems-of-werewolves-and-space-opera?p=11493#post11493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For colonization, remember the Uratha don't always breed true. Sometimes it skips a generation, sometimes it never comes up. They've been around as long as humanity has, if every child a werewolf made was a werewolf, everyone would be. Or a lot more than there are, at least. As written the Uratha are the minority, and likely always will be. So if they decided to colonize a planet there'd eventually be a disparity between normal humans outnumbering the wolf blooded and werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>An all-Uratha colony is impossible (you can't predict whether someone will go through the First Change, and they can't breed without humans), but populating a planet with only wolf-blooded humans should totally be doable. I never got the impression that wolf-bloodedness was randomly going to disappear in some of the kids of two wolf-bloods. Rather, wolf-bloods have kids with normal humans, and thus not all of their kids are wolf-bloods. There's no particular selection pressure FOR or AGAINST wolf-bloodedness (well, maybe a slight AGAINST... being kin with a werewolf can be dangerous), so if it's a minority in a population, it will stay so, and if it's dominant in a population, it will stay so. And if everyone is a wolf-blood in a population, then everyone is going to be a wolf-blood (unless there's immigration).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}